{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3155","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3155","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3155\",\"parent_revision\":\"7ed83f0b816d701598ce011237d08ab8ef406af802b3a827d1297838abbbd1b1\",\"root_revision\":\"7ed83f0b816d701598ce011237d08ab8ef406af802b3a827d1297838abbbd1b1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhile investigating #2963 (\\\"GitHub-backend issue-body reconcile: pending mutations accumulate and never drain across grooming sessions\\\"), a live reproduction was run directly against this repo's local durable cache at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/github-cache/cache.yaml` on 2026-08-23.\\n\\nObserved: the cache's `pending_work_items` queue (queued backlog-item-creation mutations, distinct from the `pending` content-write queue that #2963 documents) currently holds 66 entries, several dated 2026-08-16 \u2014 over a week stale. Cross-checking a sample of those entries' linked issue numbers against live GitHub (`gh api repos/.../issues/N`) confirms the underlying create-mutations already succeeded: #2904, #2905, and #2906 all exist on GitHub and are already `closed` (fully resolved), yet each remains present in the local `pending_work_items` queue as if still unacknowledged.\\n\\nThis is the same failure shape #2963 describes (\\\"the tool reports success but the queued mutation never drains\\\") but observed in the item-creation queue mechanism rather than the issue-body-reconcile mechanism #2963 scopes itself to. Also notable: #2963 itself is currently `closed` on GitHub despite this class of symptom remaining live-reproducible right now, which may mean #2963 was closed for one mechanism (issue-body reconcile) while a sibling mechanism (item-creation pending_work_items) was never addressed, or was closed prematurely.\\n\\nImpact: an ever-growing local pending queue that never reflects true GitHub state, inflating \\\"pending mutation\\\" counts reported by backlog_groom/reconcile operations indefinitely, and (per AGENTS.md's `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` reading trigger) matching a documented recurring failure shape \u2014 \\\"a queued mutation never gets acknowledged after the thing it was waiting for already happened\\\" \u2014 already seen multiple times in this codebase's history.\\n\\n**Research first**: `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` is flagged in this repo's AGENTS.md as required reading before diagnosing this exact recurring failure shape in `backlog_core/`; read it before tracing further. Confirm which write path is responsible for acknowledging/discarding a `pending_work_items` entry after its underlying GitHub issue creation is confirmed, and why that acknowledgement is not firing for #2904/#2905/#2906 and the other 60+ stale entries.\\n\\nRelated: #2963, #2907, #2956, #2903.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, split out of #2963\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ee8ef68b7687e67fd973f14ba09aa5ac340861a88e2699a5826fa9ba55ebf3ab\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQN36Yw\"}"}